  "instance_name": "agency_and_competence_stereotype",
  "label": "Agency and Competence Stereotype",
  "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype that certain groups (in this case, the individuals in the niqab and/or LGBTQ+ individuals) are incapable of understanding or making decisions for themselves. This is a form of ableism and misogyny, where competence and autonomy are denied to marginalized groups. The text 'or just let them figure it out for themselves?' implies that these individuals are not capable of self-determination, reinforcing a paternalistic and dismissive attitude.",
